body:
I guess this may also happen in other dialect.

> password attribute may be any object with a str method.

@zzzeek What was the use case for this?

In my specific case, I was setting up a dynamic IAM password on AWS.

This feature made it extremely easy (code a bit simplified):

```py
@dataclass
class IAMPassword:
    db_username: str
    db_host: str
    db_port: int
    db_region: str

    def __str__(self) -> str:
        client = boto3.client("rds", self.db_region)
        return client.generate_db_auth_token(
            DBHostname=self.db_host,
            Port=str(self.db_port),
            DBUsername=self.db_username,
            Region=self.db_region,
        )

    def __call__(self) -> str:
        return str(self)

```
